# Rust_Julia_FFI_Flutter_Template + Agentic layer

**Product:** Flutter-Rust-Julia FFI template with wrdlHelper (Wordle solver) as reference implementation. **iOS-first** with macOS and Android support.

**CRITICAL:** The FFI bindings between Flutter, Rust, and iOS are **fragile**. Changes to `ios/`, `rust/Cargo.toml`, `flutter_rust_bridge.yaml`, or `rust_builder/` can break the entire build. Read [docs/SETUP_GUIDE.md](docs/SETUP_GUIDE.md) before touching these.

Cursor rules, skills, handoff protocol from AgenticTemplate (manual sync — no upstream remote to protect FFI files).

**Source of truth:** [PM_PLAN.md](PM_PLAN.md), [AGENT_HANDOFF.md](AGENT_HANDOFF.md), [TECH_DEBT.md](TECH_DEBT.md), [RISKS.md](RISKS.md), [RELEASE.md](RELEASE.md), [INCIDENTS.md](INCIDENTS.md), [docs/](docs/) (SETUP_GUIDE, TESTING_STRATEGY, COMPREHENSIVE_ARCHITECTURE). Skills: [.cursor/skills/](.cursor/skills/) (DEV_GUIDE.md, TEST_TDD.md, techwriter, tester, green-and-clean, context-bootstrapper, session-summarizer, code-reviewer, code-quality-gate, tech-lead, tech-debt-evaluator, eval-engineer, risk-manager, release-manager, security-reviewer, incident-triager, pm-governance, ui-ux, game-readiness, visual-match, github-feature-workflow). **Operating model:** Use green-and-clean for scope discipline; use context-bootstrapper when starting/resuming; use session-summarizer when handing off.

**TDD:** Read TEST_TDD.md and tester skill first. **Tier 1a:** `cargo test` (Rust). **Tier 1b:** `flutter test` (Flutter). **Tier 2:** `flutter test integration_test/` (device).

**Merge-ready gate:** `cd wrdlHelper && flutter test && cd rust && cargo test && cd ..` — run before pushing to `main`.

**FFI changes:** Before modifying Rust API (`rust/src/api/*.rs`), regenerate bindings after with `flutter_rust_bridge_codegen generate`. **Never edit** `lib/src/rust/` directly — it's generated.

**Handoff:** When the user wants a handoff, run code review (code-reviewer), tech debt (tech-debt-evaluator), and tests; record in handoff note. See [.cursor/rules/handoff-checklist.mdc](.cursor/rules/handoff-checklist.mdc). **Epic close:** when an epic's in-scope work is done, run pm-governance *Epic close* automatically (includes `handoff-checklist.mdc`) � do not wait for the user to ask (`.cursor/rules/epic-close.mdc`).
